{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Landed for review as Gerrit change 1950 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1950),\ncommit 82e86cbdc3 on base fcc171c16c.\n\nEVIDENCE — the test now discriminates (AC4/AC3/AC2/AC1).\n\nInstrumentation actually fires (this was verified, not assumed). A temporary probe printing\nlen(captured) inside the test reported \"PROBE mcp composed = 1\" and\n\"PROBE reconciler composed = 1\" — so the recorder installed on the module global\nrebar._operation_config.compose_operation_snapshot is genuinely reached by code entered\nthrough the real MCP tool call and the real reconciler main(). This matters because\nemit_shadow_snapshot resolves that name from module globals at CALL time; had it been bound\nat import time the rebind would have silently no-opped and an empty capture would look\nidentical to a pass. The probe was removed; the \"composed no operation snapshot\" assertion\nis the permanent guard against that failure mode.\n\nMUT-1 — composer perturbation. Inserted into compose_operation_snapshot, immediately after\nresolve_with_sources:\n\n    sources = {\n        sect: {k: (\"project\" if v == \"env\" else v) for k, v in keys.items()}\n        for sect, keys in sources.items()\n    }\n\nRED: the new file fails —\n  AssertionError: public Python: verify.max_ticket_description_chars source\n  assert 'project' == 'env'\nWith the public-Python anchor line temporarily removed to show the surface blocks fail on\ntheir own merits, the failure moves to the MCP surface's own composed snapshot:\n  AssertionError: MCP: verify.max_ticket_description_chars source\n  assert 'project' == 'env'\n\nThe PRE-CHANGE file (origin/main's version, copied in as a second test module) passes\n5/5 GREEN under the identical perturbation. That is the direct measure of the strengthening:\nsame mutation, old test blind, new test RED.\n\nGREEN: composer reverted -> 5 passed.\n\nMUT-2 — surface perturbation. Replacing the body of _shadow in src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py\nwith a bare return, and separately the body of _emit_operation_shadow in\nsrc/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py, each turns that surface RED by name:\n  AssertionError: the MCP surface composed no operation snapshot: ...\n  AssertionError: the reconciler surface composed no operation snapshot: ...\nThe pre-change file passes 5/5 GREEN under both. Reverted -> GREEN.\n\nGATES (worktree venv, rebased onto fcc171c16c):\n  make lint            -> pass (ruff check + format-check + config/DCO/criteria/skill/zizmor/actionlint)\n  make typecheck       -> Success: no issues found in 580 source files\n  python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check  -> active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0\n  pytest tests/interfaces/contracts tests/unit/test_operation_snapshot.py\n       tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate                       -> 460 passed\n  pytest tests/interfaces/contracts tests/unit/test_operation_snapshot.py (post-rebase) -> 268 passed\n\nThe whole-tree run is deferred to CI's Verified vote on this exact commit: this host runs the\nfull suite serially in ~3 hours under multi-agent contention, and detached runs here have\nproduced errors that do not reproduce in the foreground (nonodorous-snotty-seaurchin).\n\nNOTE (not absorbed into this change, per scope): an earlier detached whole-tree run reported\ntests/integration/test_epoch_guard_reconciliation.py failing with \"Test leaked new entries\ninto REPO_ROOT\". Root cause is environmental, not this change — tests/conftest.py's\n_no_repo_root_leaks fixture snapshots REPO_ROOT per test, and concurrent `rebar edit` /\n`rebar set-file-impact` calls in this same worktree wrote .tickets-tracker under that root\nmid-run. The test passes 7/7 in isolation on the pristine base."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787206429237098001,"uuid":"3bf65905-92ca-4af1-be3c-d2283684adad"}